				<header class="comment-meta">
					
					<div class="comment-author vcard">
						<img alt="" src="https://i0.wp.com/www.techdirt.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/u5_100x0-1.jpg?resize=100%2C66&amp;ssl=1" class="avatar avatar-120 photo" height="120" width="120"><span class="fn">Mike Masnick</span> <a href="https://www.techdirt.com/user/mmasnick/" rel="external nofollow" class="url">(profile)</a> <span class="screen-reader-text says">says:</span>					</div><!-- .comment-author -->

					<div class="comment-metadata">
						<a href="https://www.techdirt.com/2023/10/05/publishing-a-book-means-no-longer-having-control-over-how-others-feel-about-it-or-how-theyre-inspired-by-it-and-that-includes-ai/#comment-5597916"><time datetime="2026-09-14T09:45:01-07:00">September 14, 2026 at 9:45 am</time></a>
					</div><!-- .comment-metadata -->

					<h1 class="comment-title">
						Re: Re: Re:<sup>3</sup> 					</h1>

				</header><!-- .comment-meta -->

				<div class="comment-content entry-content">

					<p>I ain’t reading all that. I’m happy for you though. Or sorry that it happened.</p>
<p>All I will say is that you didn’t know Aaron. I did. And for you to claim that <em>I</em> am the one misusing his legacy is insulting to me as someone who STILL sits on the board of the non-profit he founded, which continues to this day do everything we can to make his legacy real.</p>
<p>I got angry at you for daring to claim that I was somehow abusing Aaron’s legacy, a person I knew and worked with, and who invited me to help govern his non-profit. Aaron is a figment of your imagination, based on what you think you know about him. The only one misrepresenting his legacy for your own benefit is you. I knew him. And for you to accuse me of abusing his legacy is fucking insulting to me and Aaron.</p>
<p>Please go find somewhere else to spew your absolute fucking nonsense. If you want to worship Aaron’s ghost, do so somewhere else. He was a real human being, who I knew. I don’t need some clueless, reading comprehension challenged rando, to attack my integrity over a false belief of a guy you never met would think.</p>
<p>It’s great that you think Aaron is a personal saint of yours. You should maybe learn a bit more about his actual life, and not just what a 2 hour documentary said about the guy.</p>

				</div><!-- .comment-content -->

